{number: 125}
{title: O Come, O Come, Emmanuel}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [G] come, O come, Em-[C] manu-[G] el,
And ransom captive [C] Isra-[G] el,
That [Em] mourns in lonely [Am] exile [D] here
Un-[G] til the Son of [C] God ap-[G] pear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Re-[D] joice! Re-[Em] joice! Em-[C] manu-[G] el
Shall [Am] come to thee, O [D7] Isra-[G] el!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O [G] come, Thou Rod of [C] Jesse, [G] free
Thine own from Satan's [C] tyran-[G] ny;
From [Em] depths of hell Thy [Am] people [D] save
And [G] give them vict'ry [C] o'er the [G] grave.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [G] come, Thou Dayspring, [C] come and [G] cheer
Our spirits by Thine [C] advent [G] here;
And [Em] drive away the [Am] shades of [D] night,
And [G] pierce the clouds and [C] bring us [G] light!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [G] come, Thou Key of [C] David, [G] come
And open wide our [C] heavenly [G] home;
Make [Em] safe the way that [Am] leads on [D] high,
And [G] close the path to [C] mise-[G] ry.
{end_of_verse}
